>> To me having had a good dose of nroff/troff the format of the section command
>> would naturally be \section[level]{section caption}.
 .
 .
>OK - but how would you indicate "one level lower/deeper"?
>I.e., without explicitly specifying the level. Perhaps the optional
>level parameter should not only take 0..n as arguments, but + and - as well?
 .
 .
What do you think about the \section{section caption} ... \end{section} (or
something alike, it should probably also begin with \begin{section}{..} )?
This has the same advantage as the +/- approach, i.e. moving "trees" of
subsections around. O.K. its a bit more typing but it is more consistent
with the rest of LaTeX's syntax.

